direction: down

title: |md
  ### TIME_WAIT: a minisock replaces the full socket
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

full: "ESTABLISHED full socket (struct tcp_sock)" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  f_body: |md
    Holds everything:
    - send + receive queues (skbs)
    - congestion state, RTT, SACK
    - timers, socket buffers
    - full struct sock + tcp_sock

    Active closer finishes the
    FIN/ACK dance → ready for TIME_WAIT.
  |
}

carve: "tcp_time_wait() — carve a minisock" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  c_body: |md
    net/ipv4/tcp_minisocks.c:326

    tw = inet_twsk_alloc(...)
      (inet_timewait_sock.c:168)

    Copies ONLY what's needed to police
    late segments on the 4-tuple:
    - tw_rcv_nxt / tw_snd_nxt (seq)
    - tw_ts_recent (PAWS)
    - tw_rcv_wnd, tw_rcv_wscale

    No data queues or congestion-control
    state: much smaller than a full tcp_sock.
  |
}

minisock: "inet_timewait_sock in ehash" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  m_body: |md
    inet_twsk_hashdance_schedule():
    - adds minisock bind ownership
    - atomically replaces the full socket's
      ehash node on the SAME 4-tuple
    - arms tw_timer for TCP_TIMEWAIT_LEN
      (60*HZ for true TIME_WAIT)

    tcp_v4_rcv sees TCP_TIME_WAIT and calls
    tcp_timewait_state_process(): ACK, RST,
    success/drop, or a SYN eligible for a
    listener after the old minisock is removed.
  |
}

closed: "Original full socket → TCP_CLOSE, then released" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  cl_body: |md
    Same tcp_time_wait() then calls
    tcp_done(sk):
      tcp_set_state(sk, TCP_CLOSE)
      → retire the full socket; final freeing
        waits for its remaining references.

    THIS is why fentry:tcp_set_state shows
    ... -> 5 -> 7 (FIN_WAIT2 -> CLOSE),
    never -> 6. State 6 lives on the minisock,
    which tcp_set_state never touches.
  |
}

gone: "2*MSL timer fires" {
  style.fill: "#ede9fe"
  g_body: |md
    tw_timer expires → minisock unhashed
    and freed. 4-tuple is finally reusable.

    If inet_twsk_alloc hits the namespace cap
    (tcp_max_tw_buckets), it returns NULL:
    no minisock; TCPTimeWaitOverflow increments
    and the full socket still closes.
  |
}

full -> carve: "close handshake done"
carve -> minisock: "lightweight stand-in inserted"
carve -> closed: "tcp_done() retires the heavy socket"
minisock -> gone: "timer expiry"
